Status: DESIGNED - NOT BUILT. Structure specified in the Blackwell cloud-equation
materials (EQS-985), whose bench programme (EQS-986 T1-T5) is NOT EXECUTED - the
vessel's structure is conditional on that programme, stated on the face.

## 1. MISSION + CLASS
Luxury scientific vessel, occupancy 100, state-transition capable. Science-first
fit-out with hotel-class accommodation. Standalone entity (no relation asserted
to SHIP-001 or STS-001).

## 2. GEOMETRY
- Hull: cylinder, length 80.0 m, diameter 14.0 m; enclosed volume 12,315 m3
  (123.2 m3 per person - luxury class); hull area 3,826 m2; 5 decks.
- Register as one body (174,221 kg at mean density 14.15 kg/m3):
  E 115.9287 / Kd 4.1353e14 / split 16.8279 / I 99.1008.
  The vessel seats between the GAS-GAP top (16.2162) and the shell floor
  (17.7192) - a ship addressed like a dense cloud that carries its own shell.

## 3. STRUCTURE - BLACKWELL CLOUD-EQUATION MATERIALS
- Hull: CLD-MAT-1 shell-foam panels, 50 mm (skeleton split 18.0896, IN SHELL;
  bulk 100 kg/m3) - 19,132 kg.
- Decks (5): CLD-MAT-1 panels - 3,848 kg.
- Primary frame: CLD-MAT-3 address-gradient members (allocation) - 2,600 kg.
- Fairings/shades: CLD-MAT-2 stratus lattice, non-structural (allocation) - 640 kg.
- STRUCTURE TOTAL: 26,221 kg = 5.1% of an aluminium shell alone at the same
  panel thickness (516,572 kg), before that ship adds decks or frame.
- Design rules R1-R3 (EQS-985) govern: every member priced twice; depth bought
  by arrangement, never mass; environmental state is a structural input (T4).

## 4. ACCOMMODATION (100 BERTHS)
- 70 cabins: 40 singles + 30 doubles (= 100 berths), en-suite, hotel class.
- Dining hall + galley; two lounges; observatory dome (science + leisure);
  library/media; gymnasium; medical bay (4 beds); hydroponics gallery
  (food supplement + air revitalisation assist).

## 5. SCIENCE FIT-OUT (allocation 22,000 kg)
- Wet/dry laboratories (4), observatory + telescope bay, sample vault,
  computing core, workshop. External sensor booms + airlock (2 EVA-class).

## 6. LIFE SUPPORT (canon human-factors class inputs, labelled)
- O2 84 kg/day; CO2 removal 100 kg/day; water loop 300 kg/day at 90% recycle
  class; food (dry) 62 kg/day. 30-day consumables + tankage allocation
  31,000 kg. Plant allocation 18,000 kg.

## 7. POWER (budget 1,150 kW)
- Hotel/luxury 500 kW (5 kW/person); science 300 kW; life support 120 kW;
  ship systems 180 kW; transition plant standby 50 kW.
- Plant type: door D-LS3 (NOT SPECIFIED); plant mass allocation 24,000 kg.

## 8. STATE TRANSITIONS
- The vessel + contents are priced as ONE BODY. A transition changes the
  vessel's LOCATION, not its ADDRESS: M and mean density are unchanged, so
  (E, Kd, split, I) are identical before and after - CLD5's rain principle
  at ship scale, carried as the design's bookkeeping law.
- Rate: 1 transition per minute DESIGN TARGET (filed class).
- Transition plant mass allocation 15,000 kg. Mechanism: DOOR D-LS1 -
  the designer's hand, NOT SPECIFIED. No mechanism is drawn or implied.

